# Keep UI and README in sync with features

If a repo update **adds, removes, or changes a feature** (capabilities, routing, backends, modalities, tools, import/export, editors, or setup steps), do not leave the UI or README describing the old product.

Ship the docs and in-app copy in the **same change** as the code. Do not treat README or Studio/Control Panel/Viewer text as optional follow-up.

## What to update

- **README.md** — Features list, The apps table, setup sections, Control Panel effects, config excerpt, and any feature-specific section. Remove claims that are no longer true.
- **Creation Studio** — Studio Mission banner, load/basis hints, tool-mode hints.
- **Control Panel** — Field labels, picker presence, provider hints (“Studio picks Text / Image / Video…”).
- **Viewer / Archives** — Toolbar buttons, tab names, export labels, import actions, type labels.

## Examples

- Adding music generation: Mission banner and README must mention music/Lyria; Control Panel needs an Audio picker; Viewer needs Save MP3; README must not still say “text, images, and video” only.
- Removing a tool or backend: delete it from README tables, Studio/Control Panel copy, and hardcoded catalog fallbacks.
- Changing behavior (e.g. Use as Basis on a song seeds the prompt, not the MP3): say so in the Viewer/Studio hint and in README.

## Skip this for

- Pure refactors, tests, lint, or internal helpers with no user-visible behavior or setup change.
- Secret/config-only edits that do not change how the app is used.
